       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the labeled maximum for adults, which is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A single 1,700 mg dose is also above the usual per-dose limits. The limit is about 1,000 mg per dose for IR, and 850 mg is the usual dose with meals when dosing three times daily. Overdosing raises the risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWas this a typo? Here are some options within the labeled limits:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the IR maximum.\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals.** This is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **1,700 mg/day total.** This could be 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n\nTell me which regimen you want, or give me the intended dose, and I'll enter it right away."
